window.docContents[187].resolve({"/Tactics/#Logical-Foundations--Tactics___-More-Basic-Tactics--Rewriting-with-Conditional-Statements":{"contents":"\n\n\n\nexample (n m p q : Nat)\n    (h : n.double = m.double)\n    (hm : m + p = q) :\n    n + p = q := by\n  rw [double_injective n m]\n  · assumption\n  · assumption\n\n\n\n\nIf we rewrite with a conditional statement of the form\nP → a = b, then Lean tries to rewrite with a = b, and then\nasks us to prove P in a new subgoal.  If the statement has more\nthan one assumption, then we get one subgoal for each assumption.\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Tactics: More Basic Tactics","header":"7.6. Rewriting with Conditional Statements","id":"/Tactics/#Logical-Foundations--Tactics___-More-Basic-Tactics--Rewriting-with-Conditional-Statements"}});